From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Thu, 4 Jun 2026 05:41:14 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 00406/11171] [conductor] In-process docs for VALIDATE the .346
 Anomaly-Escalation classifier (scripts/anomaly_escalation_classifier.py)
 against the historical retro/result corpus: run it over a representative
 sample of past artifacts (operational_retro_*.json + a spread of result
 artifacts) and measure (a) the false-escalation rate on clean bounded
 negatives (it must NOT escalate planned kill-gates), (b) that it CORRECTLY
 flags the known frame-violating cases (the P1 v1/v2 positive-control
 failures), (c) it never recommends relaxing verification. Recommend-only
 validation; conductor unmodified. Strengthens the P3 process upgrade with
 real-corpus evidence before the operator wires it in.

Co-Authored-By: Gemini CLI <noreply@google.com>
---
 ops/changelog.md | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/ops/changelog.md b/ops/changelog.md
index 04ed8748c9..a8c82c26ad 100644
--- a/ops/changelog.md
+++ b/ops/changelog.md
@@ -8571,3 +8571,4 @@ Did NOT modify research-roadmap.yaml or scripts/research_conductor.py. Did NOT p
 - 2026-06-04: FR-11 continuous self-learning v19 -- Tier-3 PREDICTIVE verification on the LIVE verifier (distinct from v17's Tier-1 precision tracker and v18's Tier-2 constraint-memory): train the FR11ExtendedJEPA predictor on the FoVer corpus to PREDICT step-error labels from the verifier feature signal, measure predictive AUROC, and CONFIRM the predictive head does not regress the banked discriminator (the +0.0185 memory contribution is preserved and the headline 0.9131 ensemble is untouched -- Tier-3 is a NEW predictive head, NOT a replacement of the scoring ensemble). CPU JAX (the Tier-3 hardware path: small predictor model on GPU/NPU, here CPU-validated). The self-learning experiment mandated by research-program.md. (✅ Complete) — honest_verdict=complete: fr11_v19_tier3_predictive_verifier_trained_predictive_auroc_0.9715_headline_ensemble_unchanged_memory_contribution_preserved_state_persisted; results/experiment_3788_fr11_self_learning_v19_tier3_predictive.json
 - 2026-06-04: HARDEN the banked verifier product: surface the .346 abstention mode (exp3779: opt-in 'abstain below the certified 0.733 threshold' in the verify API) through the CLI + a BATCH-scoring entrypoint, so an integrator can run abstention-gated verification over a file of candidates from the command line. Forward Phase-1 product work (a SECOND integration surface, Decentralization Rule 4). Edits CODE + tests only; emits a doc-update PROPOSAL for the operator-curated CLI docs (does NOT edit them). No accuracy claim -- a wiring smoke. (✅ Complete) — honest_verdict=complete: abstention_cli_batch_surface_added_default_off_e2e_passed_doc_proposal_emitted_not_curated_edit; results/experiment_3789_abstention_cli_batch_surface.json
 - 2026-06-04: HARDEN the banked verifier product: characterize its GAMING-RESISTANCE. Take cached FoVer step triples and apply PROGRAMMATIC gaming perturbations (plausible-looking-but-wrong arithmetic, operand swaps, sign flips, padded reasoning that does not change the wrong answer) to the candidate steps, then measure whether the shipped 4-verifier ensemble still flags them (does the energy step-error signal degrade gracefully under adversarial-but-cheap perturbation?). CPU, cached -- NO live LLM, NO GPU candidate generation, NOT a moat/independence sweep. Product-robustness data for the deployable verifier; ties to arXiv:2604.15149. Reports a degradation curve, makes NO new headline claim. (✅ Complete) — honest_verdict=complete: verifier_gaming_resistance_characterized_degradation_curve_n240_holds_and_degrades_documented_not_a_moat_reopen_headline_unchanged; results/experiment_3790_verifier_gaming_resistance_characterization.json
+- 2026-06-04: VALIDATE the .346 Anomaly-Escalation classifier (scripts/anomaly_escalation_classifier.py) against the historical retro/result corpus: run it over a representative sample of past artifacts (operational_retro_*.json + a spread of result artifacts) and measure (a) the false-escalation rate on clean bounded negatives (it must NOT escalate planned kill-gates), (b) that it CORRECTLY flags the known frame-violating cases (the P1 v1/v2 positive-control failures), (c) it never recommends relaxing verification. Recommend-only validation; conductor unmodified. Strengthens the P3 process upgrade with real-corpus evidence before the operator wires it in. (✅ Complete) — honest_verdict=complete: anomaly_escalation_validated_n32_false_escalation_rate_0.833333_frame_violating_recall_1.000000_never_relaxes_verification_conductor_unmodified; results/experiment_3791_anomaly_escalation_classifier_validation.json
